  "statement_checks": "Compared all nine proposition statements and the plan's main theorem with the manuscript. The polynomial class, derivative weight, real-variable hypotheses, quantifiers, uniformity, Euler factors, three error terms, range 7/9+\u03b4 \u2264 log_x Y \u2264 1\u2212\u03b4, and exponent \u03b7 are preserved. Documented auxiliary strengthenings follow from the archived proofs. The normalization and convergence corrections to P1, P8 endpoint treatment, and corrected sawtooth arithmetic are valid. Lemma 2.6 now has the necessary improper-integral convergence hypothesis, which holds in every infinite-interval application. No brief.md was supplied.",
  "dependency_checks": "Independently checked the exact cancellation in the variance identity, the uniform M\u00f6bius truncation for squarefree pairs, the coprime-squarefree Euler product, and the weighted sawtooth convolution. Rechecked all five Euler\u2013Maclaurin remainder bounds: their sum is 449\u039b/8, consistent with c1=60. The polynomial-average argument correctly allows repeated factors and content primes through \u03c1(p\u00b2)\u2264p\u03c1(p). Its divisor tails, residue-class endpoint bounds and epsilon absorption are valid. The final assembly uses every dependency within its contract and yields the stated errors and asymptotic range. changes.md maps the results to the archived proofs and both passing reviews; those verdicts were not used as substitutes for checking the arguments.",
  "numerics_checks": "All accepted-snapshot artifact hashes, proof-file hashes, generated-artifact hashes and the PDF hash checked successfully. The shipped rerun results agree with the archive in every non-runtime field. Inspected the C++ integer autocorrelation and rational coefficient path, Python decimal accumulation, regressions, cutoff selection and heuristic uncertainty envelope. Re-executed the supplied validations and the read-only counting worker at x=250000; all 24 rows matched exactly. Independent direct residue counting verified the 16 quadratic/cubic rows there within 6.7e\u221216 relative error. Recomputed all fits, Euler products, root checks, symbolic identities and 66 exact-shape rows. Fresh in-memory generation matched all 27 generated artifacts and every non-runtime reproduction field. The identity self-test reproduced 4.783e\u221210. The full-grid compilation/rerun was verified through code and reproduce.log, rather than repeated during this read-only review. Floating-point certification and empirical-fit limitations are disclosed accurately.",
  "citation_checks": "Verified the quoted formulas in R. C. Vaughan, A variance for k-free numbers in arithmetic progressions (2005), https://doi.org/10.1112/S0024611505015352, and the cited tools in H. L. Montgomery and R. C. Vaughan, Multiplicative Number Theory I. Classical Theory (recorded as 2007), https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511618314. Checked the background directly in supplied J. Br\u00fcdern and T. D. Wooley, Sparse variance for primes in arithmetic progression (2011), and J. Br\u00fcdern, A. Granville, A. Perelli, R. C. Vaughan and T. D. Wooley, On the exponential sum over k-free numbers (1998). Verified locators for those two papers are unavailable in the supplied material, as the bibliography explicitly records. The attribution citations D. A. Goldston and R. C. Vaughan, On the Montgomery\u2013Hooley asymptotic formula (1997), https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511526091.010, and R. C. Vaughan, On a variance associated with the distribution of general sequences in arithmetic progressions. I (1998), https://doi.org/10.1098/rsta.1998.0185, agree with the supplied material. No online research or ineligible literature was used.",
  "provenance_checks": "Appendix B agrees with provenance.json on model identifiers, roles, CLI versions, repository URL, archive commit, harness commit and recorded run revision. It correctly distinguishes CLI versions from unavailable model-weight versions and makes no human-authorship claim. changes.md distinguishes archived proofs from subsequent editorial corrections and added numerical checks. Repository history was not browsed or independently authenticated. No excluded work or other-run manuscript was accessed, and no supplied file was modified.",
  "layout_checks": "Used Poppler text extraction and rendered PDF pages 3, 4, 6, 14, 19, 23\u201327 and 29\u201332. The theorem, long equations, numerical tables, three figures, bibliography and provenance are legible and complete on the inspected pages; no clipping or overlapping content was found. References and equation numbering resolve. The build log contains no undefined-reference, duplicate-destination or overfull-box warning. Visual findings come from rendered pages, not merely the log."
 }
}
