   177	\subsection{Limitations}\label{sec:num-limits}
   178	
   179	\begin{itemize}
   180	\item The computations stop at $x=2.56\cdot10^8$. With the actual ratio $\varrho=f(y)/x$, a row lies in the range $x^{7/9+\delta}\le f(y)\le x^{1-\delta}$ of \cref{thm:main}(iii) exactly when
   181	\[
   182	\delta\le\delta_{\mathrm{row}}:=\min\Bigl(\frac{\log\varrho}{\log x}+\frac29,\ -\frac{\log\varrho}{\log x}\Bigr).
   183	\]
   184	At $x=2.56\cdot10^8$ we have $x^{-2/9}\approx\XTwoNinths$. The rows with $r\le0.01$ have $\varrho\le r<x^{-2/9}$, so $\delta_{\mathrm{row}}<0$ and they lie outside the range for every $\delta>0$. The rows with $r=1$ have $\varrho$ close to $1$ and $\delta_{\mathrm{row}}\le\DeltaRowOneMax$, so they lie in the range only for very small $\delta$; the implied constant in~(iii) depends on $\delta$ and is not explicit. Over the whole grid at this $x$, $\delta_{\mathrm{row}}$ is largest, about $\DeltaRowMax$, at $r=\DeltaRowMaxR$. For each fixed $\delta>0$, the rows with a fixed target ratio $r$ leave the range as $x$ grows, since they need $x\le\varrho^{-1/\delta}$, where $\varrho\approx r$. The values of $\delta_{\mathrm{row}}$ for all rows at the largest $x$ are recorded in \texttt{reproduction.json}.
   185	\item The implied constants in \cref{thm:main} are not explicit, so no finite computation can confirm or refute it. The data can only be checked for consistency.
   186	\item The extrapolated constants depend on an empirical model, and their uncertainties are heuristic envelopes, not confidence intervals. The agreement in \cref{tab:fits} is therefore qualitative evidence for the value of $C_f$, and the theorem does not rest on it.
   187	\item The values of $C_f$ in \cref{tab:constants} come with a rigorous bound for the omitted primes, but not with a certified bound for floating-point rounding; the $40$-digit recomputation for $N=10^5$ is only a check.
   188	\item The exact-shape comparison uses double-precision arithmetic, with $80$-digit evaluation only where cancellation occurs. Its agreement with the identity self-test is the main check of the implementation. For $2k+1$ it covers only $x\le10^6$.
